<title>ARGENTINA: ARGENTINE PENSION FUNDS YIELD 26.35 PCT TO JULY.</title>
<headline>ARGENTINE PENSION FUNDS YIELD 26.35 PCT TO JULY.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's private pension funds achieved an average return of 26.35 percent on investments in the year to the end of July, the office of the Superintendent of Pension and Retirement Funds said Friday.</p>
<p>In the year to June, the funds, known by their Spanish acronym AFJPs, achieved a return of 23.48 percent.</p>
<p>The maximum return attained by a fund in the year to July was 34.26 percent, while the lowest was 18.45 percent.</p>
<p>The average annual return since the private pension funds were first established in the middle of 1994 was 19.87 percent.</p>
<p>((--Jorge Otaola, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0651))</p>
